            "advisory": "Affected versions of the `PyJWT` package are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception due to a plain `ValueError` raised while parsing a malformed RSA key escaping the per-key error handling of JWK Set parsing. `PyJWK.__init__` calls `RSAAlgorithm.from_jwk` without catching errors, and when an RSA JWK supplies `d`, `e` and `n` with an incorrect private exponent and no CRT parameters, `rsa_recover_prime_factors` raises a `ValueError` that is not a `PyJWTError` and therefore is not skipped by the `except PyJWTError` guard in `PyJWKSet.__init__`. An attacker who can place one malformed key in a JWK Set that an application parses, for example through `PyJWKSet.from_dict` or `PyJWKClient.get_jwk_set`, can abort parsing of the entire set so that no valid key is loaded, breaking token verification for every key in that set.",
