            "advisory": "Affected versions of the `PyJWT` package are vulnerable to Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature due to an incomplete guard against using an asymmetric public key as an HMAC secret. `HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key` only rejects asymmetric keys when `is_pem_format` or `is_ssh_key` recognizes them, but the `is_pem_format` regular expression rejects PEM forms with whitespace next to the markers, CR-only line terminators or a single folded line that `cryptography` still loads as a valid public key, so such a key is returned unchanged and used as the HMAC secret. When `jwt.decode` is called with an allow-list that mixes an HMAC algorithm with an asymmetric one and the key is passed as raw PEM text in one of these forms, an attacker who knows the public key can sign an `HS256` token with it and forge arbitrary claims that the application accepts as valid.",
