            "advisory": "Affected versions of the `PyJWT` package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling due to `PyJWKClient` forcing a fresh JWKS fetch for every unknown `kid` value with no rate limit, negative cache or minimum refresh interval. The `get_signing_key` method calls `get_signing_keys(refresh=True)` on any unknown `kid`, which bypasses `jwk_set_cache` and calls `fetch_data()`, and because the `kid` is read from the unverified token header by `get_signing_key_from_jwt`, even a repeated unknown value triggers a new fetch on every call. An unauthenticated attacker can flood an application with tokens carrying arbitrary `kid` values, making the server issue one outbound JWKS request and JSON parse per token, exhausting its CPU and sockets and potentially tripping the identity provider's rate limit, which causes an application-wide authentication outage.",
